# 02 Data Synchronization Strategy

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant LS as 💾 LocalStorage
    participant SE as 🔄 Sync Engine
    participant API as 📡 REST API
    participant DB as 🏠 Database

    Note over LS, DB: Phase 1: Client Synchronization
    SE->>LS: Get local-clients
    LS-->>SE: Array[Client]
    loop Each Client
        SE->>API: POST /api/clients
        API->>DB: create(client)
        DB-->>API: New UUID
        API-->>SE: New UUID
        SE->>SE: Map: LocalID -> NewUUID
    end

    Note over LS, DB: Phase 2: Project Inheritance
    SE->>LS: Get local-projects
    LS-->>SE: Array[Project]
    loop Each Project
        SE->>SE: Update ClientID from Map
        SE->>API: POST /api/projects
        API->>DB: create(project)
        DB-->>API: New ProjectUUID
        API-->>SE: New ProjectUUID
        SE->>SE: Map: LocalProjectID -> ProjectUUID
    end

    Note over LS, DB: Phase 3: Cleanup
    SE->>LS: Clear flowshan-* keys
```

### Story: Maintaining Relationship Integrity
The most critical part of the sync is not just moving data, but **preserving relationships**. By mapping old IDs to new UUIDs in memory during the process, we ensure that a Task created locally still knows which Project it belongs to once they both live on the server.
